Z||000000||LAMBO||08-30-2001||09:38 AM||||My ailing 84 SE dukie has a bad ticker.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84se_3.jpg"> <BR>So I've decided to give it a heart transplant.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/caddymotor.jpg"> <BR>And it only cost me $500 for the whole donor cradle, motor/tranny/harness/computer. The 84 should feel all better when I'm through, 200hp, 275ft/lbs torque. I'd better get out and get started. Need to get that 2m8 sticker ordered too. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||skitime||08-30-2001||10:16 AM||||Lambo, Do me a favor and document your work.  I want to do much the same thing too.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||LAMBO||08-30-2001||01:01 PM||||Skitime,<BR>I do plan to document as much as possible. I have several decisions to make in terms of mounting, which tranny to use, things of that nature. So far, I only have $800 in the SE with disassembled duke and the 4.9 Caddy/4t60-E tranny on cradle. Between Rockcrawl and Bubbajoe as information resources (ie, websites), I should be able to finish this project without much more in major expenses. Just little things like gaskets and seals, some wiring stuff, simple exhaust, things like that. I'm really sold on this engine swap, especially for all the ducks out there. You can find these engines all day long in the junk yards for $400 to $650 with reasonable miles on them (less than 80K). And, you don't need a conversion kit to put them in. Hardest part for me will be splicing in the forward Fiero harness, just because I'm a little intimidated by electrical stuff. But I'm going for it, can't wait to here that V8 rumble.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||08-30-2001||01:16 PM||||What sites have info on that swap???  I am interested in reading about it.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||08-30-2001||01:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LAMBO:<BR><B>Skitime,<BR>I do plan to document as much as possible. Todd</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Lambo, great to hear that you plan to document your work.  That will be an asset to the whole forum. Both Rockcrawl and Bubbajoe have done the 4.5 V8 I believe.  I know the 4.9 has been done by others so be sure to document the 4.9 differences.  Luckily, I live fairly close to Rockcrawl and have spoken to him about his install and plan to get up to see it. He says it looks like it appears as if it was in from factory.  So which trans?  My car is automatic but I have a complete 88 Fiero engine, 5 speed Getrag and cradle (pedals, shifter cables and wiring harness too) sitting in the garage enticing me to convert to the 5 speed.  Wish you were not so far away or I would come over and give you a hand so I could learn along the way.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LAMBO||08-30-2001||01:29 PM||||Fieromaster88<BR>Check here: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> <BR>and here: <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/index.htm</A> <P>Skitime, I wish you weren't so far away either. I wouldn't mind the help. The only 4.9's that I've heard of being successful using the stock Caddy ECM are 5 speed manuals. I'm going to try the 4sp auto that came with the 4.9 as I think it will be a little better (and I want the OD for highway cruising) than the 125 in the car now. Plus I dont' have to shell out for a mini starter or notch out the bell houseing to accept the larger Caddy starter. This project is a test and learn on the 84, as I plan on doing the same swap in my 88 hybrid, except it'll be a 5 speed.<BR>Todd<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LAMBO (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||08-30-2001||02:02 PM||||WOOHOOO! I'm glad to see someone else jump on this project. For some reason, it seems this is the most overlooked motor swap out there. Lots of 3.4 (both push rod and DOHC) 3800, 3800SC, SMB and N*. But, for some reason, there are a LOT of doubters out there regarding this swap. I've researched the installation so I'm kind of OK on that. What I want to hear is you FIRST IMPRESSIONS regarding acceleration and handling. And, if yu have time and a little extra $$$, I'd love to see a dyno pull.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Please, keep us posted<P><BR>------------------<BR>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||AusFiero||08-30-2001||05:46 PM||||Is that all it cost for those motors? sheez thats cheaper than rebuilding a Fiero motor over here even after it is converted to AU$$$s and shipped and taxed. Hmm So where do I find one of those babies?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000008||SteveJ||08-30-2001||06:47 PM||||Love that engine. I have one in the Deville out in my garage. It is one fine engine. Mine has 90,000 on it and the oil stays clean between changes. The computer tells you when to change oil which turns out to be about 7000 miles, but still the oil is clean. Power seems unlimited. I have never had to floor it because it always had plenty. Mine is a '95 and a bit of a hybrid. It takes crank and cam signals from the distributor. <BR>The trans is great. I love it. It freewheels at speed if you take your foot off. I get 24 mpg on the road with the Deville body on it.<P>Yer gunna love it. What year is the engine?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by SteveJ (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||LAMBO||08-31-2001||08:59 AM||||Steve,<BR>The motor is a '91. I think there is still a little untapped potential in these motors above and beyond the factory rated hp and torque. The computers have a 4500 rev limit and a top speed of 115. With an aftermarket computer or something like a Camaro ECM (something thats been hacked already), I bet theres another 20 to 30 hp to be had. Rockcrawl is playing with a Camaro ECM right now on a 4.5 pfi motor. He hasn't said much about what he's been able to do, but he's definatly not having to deal with the limiters. I'm going to use the stock ECM because I'm probably going to use the 4t60-E tranny and I want it to work properly. When I go to do my 88 with a 5sp., I might try another ECM. Maybe Rockcrawl will have the Camaro one figured out by then and I can go that route.<P>mrfixit58, I will see what I can do on the dyno numbers. Not many in my area. Probably have to wait for one of those traveling ones to come thru in a car show or something.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
